What is Docker and why every DevOps/SRE should understand its internals?
Docker is more than just docker run.

 Understanding its core components helps you debug faster, design better pipelines, and build truly portable systems.

🔹 Docker Client – Where commands start (build, run, stop)

 🔹 Docker Daemon – The engine that builds, runs, and manages containers

 🔹 Dockerfile – The recipe that defines how your image is built

 🔹 Docker Hub – Registry to store and share container images

👉 Knowing how these pieces work together matters far more than memorizing commands.

If you’re working with containers daily, this is a must-know foundation.
